  "lyrics": [
    {
      "start": 0.05,
      "end": 3.611,
      "text": "A schema does not appear fully formed in CREATE TABLE.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 3.611,
      "end": 6.75,
      "text": "It moves through three views of the same idea.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 6.75,
      "end": 10.902,
      "text": "Conceptual design names the things and how they relate.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 10.902,
      "end": 13.097,
      "text": "Customer, order, book.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 13.097,
      "end": 15.486,
      "text": "A customer places many orders.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 15.486,
      "end": 17.763,
      "text": "An order contains many books.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 17.763,
      "end": 22.055,
      "text": "You can sketch this with boxes and lines, or with sentences.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 22.055,
      "end": 23.277,
      "text": "No types yet.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 23.277,
      "end": 24.666,
      "text": "No indexes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 24.666,
      "end": 30.138,
      "text": "Logical design turns those things into tables, keys, and constraints.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 30.138,
      "end": 32.375,
      "text": "Now you choose primary keys.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 32.375,
      "end": 34.069,
      "text": "You add foreign keys.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 34.069,
      "end": 36.722,
      "text": "You decide which attributes are NOT NULL.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 36.722,
      "end": 39.791,
      "text": "You normalize so each table has one job.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 39.791,
      "end": 44.75,
      "text": "Physical design is how a particular engine stores and finds the rows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 44.75,
      "end": 46.208,
      "text": "Types get sharper.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 46.208,
      "end": 47.638,
      "text": "Indexes appear.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 47.638,
      "end": 51.416,
      "text": "Partitioning, files, and memory settings live here.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 51.416,
      "end": 56.694,
      "text": "If you start physical, you will pick VARCHAR forty because a form looked forty wide.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 56.694,
      "end": 58.694,
      "text": "That is not a conceptual reason.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 58.694,
      "end": 62.486,
      "text": "Keep the conceptual sketch next to the CREATE statements.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 62.486,
      "end": 66.958,
      "text": "When they disagree, the sketch wins until you update it on purpose.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 66.958,
      "end": 68.527,
      "text": "Requirements change.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 68.527,
      "end": 71.472,
      "text": "A bookstore starts lending, not only selling.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 71.472,
      "end": 75.347,
      "text": "That is a new relationship, not a new column on orders.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 75.347,
      "end": 77.208,
      "text": "Walk the three views again.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 77.208,
      "end": 78.777,
      "text": "Name the new entity.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 78.777,
      "end": 80.263,
      "text": "Place it on the sketch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 80.263,
      "end": 81.625,
      "text": "Then give it a table.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 81.625,
      "end": 83.513,
      "text": "Then decide how it is stored.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 83.513,
      "end": 87.125,
      "text": "Teams skip the sketch because SQL feels like progress.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 87.125,
      "end": 91.736,
      "text": "Progress without a sketch is a pile of columns named extra1.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 91.736,
      "end": 94.069,
      "text": "Document the keys in the sketch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 94.069,
      "end": 98.458,
      "text": "Document the verbs: places, contains, borrows.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 98.458,
      "end": 102.055,
      "text": "Then the SQL has a source of truth besides memory.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 102.055,
      "end": 104.277,
      "text": "Review is part of the lifecycle.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 104.277,
      "end": 108.0,
      "text": "A second person should try to query a question from the sketch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 108.0,
      "end": 111.013,
      "text": "If they cannot, the sketch is unfinished.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 111.013,
      "end": 114.819,
      "text": "Migration is the lifecycle continuing after launch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 114.819,
      "end": 117.694,
      "text": "ALTER is not a failure of the first design.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 117.694,
      "end": 120.222,
      "text": "It is the design meeting a new fact.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 120.222,
      "end": 122.041,
      "text": "Still start from the sketch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 122.041,
      "end": 125.833,
      "text": "Physical tricks come last, after the keys are honest.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 125.833,
      "end": 127.888,
      "text": "That order is the lifecycle.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 127.888,
      "end": 129.625,
      "text": "Tools will try to skip a view.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 129.625,
      "end": 136.138,
      "text": "An ORM that emits tables from classes is a logical step wearing a programming language.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 136.138,
      "end": 140.583,
      "text": "It still needs a conceptual sketch, or the classes will be screens.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 140.583,
      "end": 142.458,
      "text": "Screens are not entities.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 142.458,
      "end": 147.0,
      "text": "A checkout page can show customer, cart, and tax at once.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 147.0,
      "end": 149.652,
      "text": "That is three entities, maybe four.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 149.652,
      "end": 154.013,
      "text": "If you start from the page, you get one wide table named checkout.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 154.013,
      "end": 155.069,
      "text": "Resist.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 155.069,
      "end": 157.944,
      "text": "Reverse engineering is a lifecycle too.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 157.944,
      "end": 163.305,
      "text": "When you inherit a database, sketch what it actually is, not what you wish it were.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 163.305,
      "end": 166.013,
      "text": "Then decide which wish is a migration.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 166.013,
      "end": 167.402,
      "text": "Version the sketch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 167.402,
      "end": 171.152,
      "text": "A picture in a slide deck from last year is not versioned.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 171.152,
      "end": 173.527,
      "text": "A file next to the migrations is.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 173.527,
      "end": 179.5,
      "text": "Physical design includes collation, fillfactor, and tablespaces in some engines.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 179.5,
      "end": 182.194,
      "text": "You can ignore them while the keys are wrong.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 182.194,
      "end": 185.361,
      "text": "You cannot ignore them forever on a large cluster.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 185.361,
      "end": 186.805,
      "text": "That is still last.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 186.805,
      "end": 188.652,
      "text": "The lifecycle is a loop.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 188.652,
      "end": 195.083,
      "text": "New requirement, new sketch mark, new logical change, new physical tweak if needed.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 195.083,
      "end": 198.652,
      "text": "Skipping the first two is how extra1 is born.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 198.652,
      "end": 203.069,
      "text": "Keep the loop boring and the tables stay dull in the best way.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 203.069,
      "end": 204.888,
      "text": "Dull tables are queryable.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 204.888,
      "end": 207.236,
      "text": "That was the point of walking in order.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 207.236,
      "end": 210.694,
      "text": "A skipped conceptual hour becomes a month of ALTER.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 210.694,
      "end": 213.041,
      "text": "That trade is almost never worth it.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 213.041,
      "end": 216.208,
      "text": "Write three sentences before three tables.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 216.208,
      "end": 220.611,
      "text": "What exists, how it relates, what must never duplicate.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 220.611,
      "end": 223.444,
      "text": "Those sentences are the conceptual design.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 223.444,
      "end": 226.888,
      "text": "Logical design is only spelling them in keys.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 226.888,
      "end": 229.708,
      "text": "Physical design is only storing them.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 229.708,
      "end": 234.152,
      "text": "If you cannot find the three sentences, you are not ready for CREATE.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 234.152,
      "end": 235.93,
      "text": "Find them, then type.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 235.93,
      "end": 239.041,
      "text": "Most failed databases were not failed SQL.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 239.041,
      "end": 241.055,
      "text": "They were skipped conversations.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 241.055,
      "end": 252.444,
      "text": "Professionals gather requirements, then shape a conceptual picture, then a logical schema, then a physical one, then they load data and check that the questions still work.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 252.444,
      "end": 256.916,
      "text": "Requirement gathering is talking to the people who will live with the data.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 256.916,
      "end": 263.402,
      "text": "Owners, staff who enter rows, people who answer customers, people who write the application.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 263.402,
      "end": 265.597,
      "text": "Each group gets different questions.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 265.597,
      "end": 267.416,
      "text": "What must never be lost.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 267.416,
      "end": 269.444,
      "text": "What must never be duplicated.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 269.444,
      "end": 274.319,
      "text": "What a day of work looks like in names of things, not in screen mockups only.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 274.319,
      "end": 276.805,
      "text": "Study the old system if there is one.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 276.938,
      "end": 281.957,
      "text": "Sample files, spreadsheets, and reports are requirements in disguise.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 281.957,
      "end": 286.276,
      "text": "Write down whether you will record interviews, and get permission if you will.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 286.276,
      "end": 290.193,
      "text": "A prompt to a language model can suggest interview questions.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 290.193,
      "end": 292.304,
      "text": "It cannot attend the meeting for you.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 292.304,
      "end": 295.165,
      "text": "You still have to hear the nouns they actually use.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 295.165,
      "end": 304.36,
      "text": "Conceptual design turns those nouns into entities and relationships, often as an ER sketch, before types exist.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 304.36,
      "end": 311.235,
      "text": "If you cannot say what exists and how it relates in three sentences, you are not ready for CREATE TABLE.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 311.235,
      "end": 317.026,
      "text": "Logical design chooses keys, attributes, and tables that implement that sketch.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 317.026,
      "end": 322.749,
      "text": "This is where primary keys, foreign keys, and normal forms earn their keep.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 322.749,
      "end": 328.165,
      "text": "Physical design chooses types, indexes, and engine-specific storage.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 328.165,
      "end": 329.901,
      "text": "It is last on purpose.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 329.901,
      "end": 334.832,
      "text": "A beautiful index on a table that should not exist is a fast mistake.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 334.832,
      "end": 338.999,
      "text": "Implementation is CREATE, load, and constraint.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 338.999,
      "end": 346.415,
      "text": "Validation is: insert the ugly cases, run the questions from the interviews, and watch for anomalies.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 346.415,
      "end": 352.624,
      "text": "If a report from week one of gathering cannot be written as SQL, the schema is not done.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 352.624,
      "end": 355.735,
      "text": "Skipping conceptual work feels like speed.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 355.735,
      "end": 357.776,
      "text": "It becomes a month of ALTER.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 357.776,
      "end": 360.429,
      "text": "Skipping validation feels like shipping.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 360.429,
      "end": 363.651,
      "text": "It becomes two sources of truth in production.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 363.651,
      "end": 366.888,
      "text": "The lifecycle is a loop when the business changes.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 366.888,
      "end": 374.61,
      "text": "You gather again, you sketch again, you migrate with ALTER instead of pretending the first CREATE was eternal.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 374.61,
      "end": 380.957,
      "text": "Write three sentences: what exists, how it relates, what must never duplicate.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 380.957,
      "end": 381.915,
      "text": "Then type.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 381.915,
      "end": 383.499,
      "text": "Not the other way around.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 383.499,
      "end": 387.04,
      "text": "Walk the store through the three big steps, slowly.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 387.04,
      "end": 393.013,
      "text": "Requirements: owners say they sell products, take reviews, and refund by order.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 393.013,
      "end": 398.401,
      "text": "Staff say they retype emails because the old spreadsheet allowed two Mayas.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 398.401,
      "end": 403.179,
      "text": "Developers say they need a user id for login that is not the email.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 403.179,
      "end": 406.013,
      "text": "Those are requirements, not tables yet.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 406.013,
      "end": 413.79,
      "text": "Conceptual: product, user, order, review, refund as boxes, verbs between them.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 413.79,
      "end": 414.929,
      "text": "No types.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 414.929,
      "end": 417.193,
      "text": "No VARCHAR 255.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 417.193,
      "end": 423.888,
      "text": "Logical: keys on each box, review points at product and user, refund points at order.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 423.888,
      "end": 427.707,
      "text": "Normal forms applied until names live in one place.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 427.707,
      "end": 437.221,
      "text": "Physical: INTEGER ids, DECIMAL prices, TIMESTAMPTZ for placed_at if the engine has it, indexes on foreign keys.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 437.221,
      "end": 441.443,
      "text": "Implement: CREATE in dependency order, parents first.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 441.443,
      "end": 449.013,
      "text": "Load a dozen ugly rows: two reviews on one product, a refund, a user with no orders.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 449.013,
      "end": 457.526,
      "text": "Validate: can you list reviews for a product, refunds for an order, and refuse a review with a fake product_id.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 457.526,
      "end": 464.638,
      "text": "If any interview question from day one cannot run, you are still in logical design, not in production.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 464.638,
      "end": 470.249,
      "text": "Generative tools can draft interview questions and even draft CREATE statements.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 470.249,
      "end": 473.624,
      "text": "They cannot sit with the staff who retype emails.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 473.624,
      "end": 479.165,
      "text": "That conversation is the step that fails when teams open a SQL window first.",
      "slide": ""
    },
    {
      "start": 479.165,
      "end": 481.638,
      "text": "Do not open the SQL window first.",
      "slide": ""
    }
  ]
}
